<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Caucasus Army of Islam</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1918">1918</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Islamic Army of the Caucasus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus">Caucasus</a> Army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> was an Ottoman force formed in 1918 under Nuri Pasha, combining Ottoman troops with Azerbaijani volunteers, to advance into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-caucasus">South Caucasus</a> after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>'s collapse. It defeated the forces of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baku">Baku</a> Commune and then of the Centrocaspian Dictatorship and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dunsterforce">Dunsterforce</a>, capturing Baku on 15 September 1918, followed by massacres of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenians">Armenians</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armistice-of-mudros">Armistice of Mudros</a> forced its withdrawal.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/caucasus-army-of-islam.jpg" alt="Caucasus Army of Islam" width="320" height="184" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Soldiers_of_Islamic_Army_of_Caucasus_near_Baku_during_battle_for_the_city_in_1918.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
